WEBVTT

00:00:00.015 --> 00:00:04.003
Easy Greek Myths. King Midas and the Golden Touch.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:08.448
Midas was a king who loved gold more than anything in the world.

00:00:08.448 --> 00:00:12.197
He had rooms full of it, but he always wanted more.

00:00:12.197 --> 00:00:15.270
One day he helped a friend of one of the gods.

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.914
The god was pleased.

00:00:16.914 --> 00:00:21.215
"Ask for anything you want," he said, "and I will give it to you."

00:00:21.215 --> 00:00:25.549
"I wish that everything I touch would turn to gold," said Midas.

00:00:25.549 --> 00:00:28.477
"That is not a wise wish," said the god.

00:00:28.477 --> 00:00:30.066
"But you shall have it."

00:00:30.066 --> 00:00:32.253
Midas could not wait to try.

00:00:32.253 --> 00:00:35.185
He touched a stone, and it turned to gold.

00:00:35.185 --> 00:00:37.401
He touched a tree and a chair.

00:00:37.401 --> 00:00:38.147
Gold!

00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:41.769
He ran through his house, laughing and touching everything.

00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:43.235
Then he was hungry.

00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:46.821
He sat down at the table and picked up a piece of bread.

00:00:46.821 --> 00:00:49.042
It turned to gold in his hand.

00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:53.438
He tried to drink some water, and it became gold in his mouth.

00:00:53.438 --> 00:00:55.774
Midas began to feel afraid.

00:00:55.774 --> 00:00:58.748
Just then his little daughter ran into the room.

00:00:58.748 --> 00:01:00.850
She put her arms around him.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.147
And before he could stop her, she turned into a gold statue.

00:01:05.147 --> 00:01:06.676
The king cried out.

00:01:06.676 --> 00:01:08.273
He ran to the god.

00:01:08.273 --> 00:01:11.602
"Please take this terrible present away," he said.

00:01:11.602 --> 00:01:13.280
"I do not want gold.

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:14.558
I want my daughter."

00:01:14.558 --> 00:01:17.455
"Go and wash in the river," said the god.

00:01:17.455 --> 00:01:20.243
Midas ran to the river and jumped in.

00:01:20.243 --> 00:01:22.599
The gold touch was washed away.

00:01:22.599 --> 00:01:26.812
He carried water back to his house and poured it over his daughter.

00:01:26.812 --> 00:01:29.167
She opened her eyes and smiled.

00:01:29.167 --> 00:01:33.877
From that day on, King Midas did not care about gold at all.
